{"title":"1973 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/4/22406bacb4253af814078fbf3cb7e5cb4aee6b13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(i)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"17\" /> Solve the simultaneous inequalities, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/8/048f10b8920017df56f7c784d1f3c7cb51ca77a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&lt;\\frac{1}{4x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"56\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/6/cd6ee81a7a535d87853e848c77654cc36104a75e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />; i.e. find a single inequality equivalent to the two simultaneous inequalities.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/c/0ac3c778e6a0a8e6b77ba3855ca818e759d27013.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(ii)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> What is the greatest integer that satisfies both inequalities <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/5/725d470599c101edeffb95a4f5c3aad8024bf808.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4x+13 &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"92\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/b/09b211e7637a4e74ce29e5aa82c7ca080b9d00ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2}+3x &gt; 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"101\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/c/9dc162a980119098c0f7c354a9a866879b37bc47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(iii)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"25\" height=\"17\" /> Give a rational number between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/6/fe6dd13274a6c9fd355416953e62f9e8677136c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11/24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/f/5df2b356b86c357291ddc3bffbed1a6cd03d4f21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6/13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/a/fba755b2bf0c4300e523c82992887f4243d6dccc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(iv)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"25\" height=\"17\" /> Express <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/1/7f1c9cc35374b57f3e393a898263c4cda825e912.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100000$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"53\" height=\"13\" /> as a product of two integers neither of which is an integral multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/c/96ca28500f069481646cdd51f5823b8a110ddf42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(v)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> Without the use of logarithm tables evaluate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/2/1a256b1384edfe17315899209cc775c1cfcab7ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{\\log_{2}36}+\\frac{1}{\\log_{3}36}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"133\" height=\"41\" />. \t\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/4/22406bacb4253af814078fbf3cb7e5cb4aee6b13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(i)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"17\" /> </p><center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/b/49b32524592c34161cab5fd7909a01e6f65080f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&lt;\\frac{1}{4x} \\Rightarrow 4x^2 &gt; 1 \\Rightarrow x^2&gt; \\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"228\" height=\"37\" />. \n<p>Since from the second inequality <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/6/cd6ee81a7a535d87853e848c77654cc36104a75e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />, our solution is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/8/fd8b0bbf8b6953c91258ead7b4b5865ed7835617.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&lt;-1/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/c/0ac3c778e6a0a8e6b77ba3855ca818e759d27013.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(ii)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> From <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/5/725d470599c101edeffb95a4f5c3aad8024bf808.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4x+13 &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"92\" height=\"14\" />, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/4/324dd3aeb4fa91425feed899c861b14dbc611dab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4x+13 &lt; 0 \\Rightarrow x &lt; -\\frac{13}{4} \\approx -3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"239\" height=\"38\" />. From  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/b/09b211e7637a4e74ce29e5aa82c7ca080b9d00ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2}+3x &gt; 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"101\" height=\"16\" />, we get: <center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/7/19788ea1133f5623218c1328f38b304d29be09d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2}+3x &gt; 16 \\Rightarrow x^{2}+3x - 16 &gt; 0 \\Rightarrow x &gt; \\frac{-3 + \\sqrt{71}}{2} \\approx 2 \\text{ or } x &lt; \\frac{-3-\\sqrt{71}}{2}\\approx -5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"632\" height=\"41\" /> </center>\n<p>With these two inequalities, we see that the greatest integer satisfying the requirements is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/e/4be006c22a04ed9e687afbe6481a9297c9541ef1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{-6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"35\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/c/9dc162a980119098c0f7c354a9a866879b37bc47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(iii)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"25\" height=\"17\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/9/3c9a27dba7da3e905f81be90e4e0c0e24c67047e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{11}{24} = \\frac{286}{624},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"81\" height=\"38\" />  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/9/8b9d7028c533dd0e301b9f929fcc8c3b238e7236.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{6}{13} = \\frac{288}{624}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"76\" height=\"38\" />. Thus, a rational number in between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/6/fe6dd13274a6c9fd355416953e62f9e8677136c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11/24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/f/5df2b356b86c357291ddc3bffbed1a6cd03d4f21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6/13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/0/650c2a1a3400b58db5e53c5b3908d216f3ddaf9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\frac{287}{624}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"46\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/a/fba755b2bf0c4300e523c82992887f4243d6dccc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(iv)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"25\" height=\"17\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/2/0f2edc19d99c1aeafc313f2eade7a855e85b006a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100000 = 10 \\times 10 \\times10 \\times10 \\times 10 = 2^{5}\\times5^{5} = 32\\times3125.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"442\" height=\"15\" /> \nThus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/1/7e191be94977fbafb0e36f579e44426a4b4e992e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100000 = \\boxed{32\\times3125}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"170\" height=\"24\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/c/96ca28500f069481646cdd51f5823b8a110ddf42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(v)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> <center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/8/558ba4a1cb3d96962f07239ec867893cbbda350e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\begin{matrix} \\frac{1}{\\log_{2}36}+\\frac{1}{\\log_{3}36} &amp;=&amp; \\log_{36}2+\\log_{36}3 \\\\  &amp;=&amp; \\log_{36}{2\\times3} \\\\  &amp;=&amp; \\log_{36}6 \\\\ &amp;=&amp; \\boxed{\\frac{1}{2}} \\end{matrix}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -51px\" width=\"277\" height=\"112\" /> \n</p>\n</center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_Canadian_MO\" title=\"1973 Canadian MO\">1973 Canadian MO</a></li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_Canadian_MO\" title=\"1973 Canadian MO\">1973 Canadian MO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_Canadian_MO_Problems\" title=\"1973 Canadian MO Problems\">Problems</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_Canadian_MO_Problems\" title=\"1973 Canadian MO Problems\">1973 Canadian MO Problems</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1973 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1973 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1973 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1973 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1973 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1973 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 7\">7</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1973 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><br />\n</p></center>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017114939\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.027 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.069 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 208/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 843/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 71/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6929/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   37.022      1 Template:Old_CanadaMO_box_(6-8_Problems)/7\n100.00%   37.022      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-w